UnixLib as a shared library (riscos-unixlib)
============================================

Version VERSION, from riscos-unixlib TAG.

riscos-unixlib is an unofficial fork of GCCSDK's UnixLib. It is not made,
released or supported by the GCCSDK developers. Please report problems at
https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-unixlib/issues, not to GCCSDK. AI
(Anthropic's Claude) has been used as a coding assistant on this fork.

STATUS
What it is
----------
lib.armeabihf.libunixlib/so/5 is UnixLib VERSION built as a shared
library, for programs that are linked dynamically and loaded through
SOManager, such as Iris. It is built from the same source as the
libunixlib.a of the same release. Compared with GCCSDK's UnixLib it has,
among other things:
  - threads and signals on RISC OS for Linux;
  - shared memory with ARMEABISupport 1.08 as well as 1.05;
  - semaphores that sleep (sem_wait, sem_timedwait);
  - the thread ticker kept running through Wimp_Poll, from code outside
    the program.
The release's CHANGELOG lists everything.

It replaces GCCSDK's libunixlib/so/5. It exports every symbol of
GCCSDK's (the same names, types and data sizes; checked when it is
built), so programs built against GCCSDK's library run with it unchanged.

Trace.lib.armeabihf.libunixlib/so/5 is the same library with a diagnostic
added: each failing call on one of ARMEABISupport's fds (shared memory,
shared files) writes a line to the program's stderr, like

  UnixLib FdOp: __armeabi_fd_fstat fd 1003: error &81DC28 ... (from &xxxxxxxx)

giving the fd, the error and the address close(), fstat() etc. were
called from. Use it only to find a problem; it is not for everyday use.

Important: one copy is shared by every program
----------------------------------------------
SOManager loads one libunixlib/so/5 for all dynamically linked programs.
Whichever !SharedLibs is in use (Iris's own sets the SharedLibs path for
the whole machine once it has been seen), every dynamically linked
program uses the copy in it. So:
  - keep the old file, so you can go back;
  - reboot after swapping it, so nothing still has the old one loaded;
  - if anything else misbehaves, swap the old file back and reboot.

Installing
----------
1. Find the libunixlib/so/5 that is used. For Iris it is inside
   !Iris.SharedLibs.!SharedLibs.lib.armeabihf (use Shift-double-click to
   open the applications). It may be called libunixlib/so/5/0/0, with
   libunixlib/so/5 linked to it; replace the one that holds the library.
2. Rename that file to libunixlib/so/5-gccsdk (don't delete it).
3. Copy lib.armeabihf.libunixlib/so/5 (or the Trace one) from this
   package into the same directory, under the same name.
4. Reboot, then run Iris.

To go back: delete the new file, rename libunixlib/so/5-gccsdk back, and
reboot.

Tests
-----
Tests contains some of UnixLibTests' programs, linked dynamically against
this library. Run them after installing; each must print PASS (Fault must
end with "Fatal signal received: Illegal instruction"). The first line of
Shm says which ARMEABISupport it found. They need SOManager and the
SharedLibs (including libm/so/1), as Iris does.

